{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum","id":157105,"title":"Super-Science in Trinity Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-02T17:19:26-07:00","id":157105,"title":"Super-Science in Trinity Continuum","content":"What I\u2019d like to see TC do with Super-Science:<br /> <br /> Make it available in all eras; but split it into different types, the same way characters are. In fact, have the super-science types mirror the character types:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Noetic Superscience emulates and enhances psychomorphic powers; it tends to fall into \u201csubtypes\u201d that individual Psion Orders specialize in; and so on. It isn\u2019t exclusive to Psions; but Psions tend to have an edge in designing and using it. Incorporate elements of <b>Trinity</b>\u2019s \u201cbio-tech\u201d into Noetic Science, such as the ability/need to bond Noetic gadgets to their owners. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Quantum Super-Science emulates and enhances Quantum Powers; it tends to be very individualistic and hard to replicate, and tends to have odd quirks. While it isn\u2019t exclusive to Novas, it tends to be hard for anyone but its inventor to use, unless he has made a concerted effort to make it user-friendly for others. That said, it is not the exclusive domain of Novas: Talents and Psions can dabble in it, too; they just have difficulty doing so (psions moreso than Talents). <br /> <br /> \u2022 Where Quantum and Noetic Super-Science represent different kinds of what <b>Adventure!</b> called Innovations, Talents specialize in a form of Super-Science that features what <b>Adventure!</b> called Advancements: gadgets that don\u2019t operate on any sort of exotic principles, but which perform better than they have any right to: a car that has unrealistically high acceleration and top speed, and/or which gets hundreds of miles per gallon; armor which withstands damage that it has no right to withstand; weapons with unbelievable accuracy and/or power; and so on. In short, \u201crubber science\u201d. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:38:59-07:00","id":157133,"title":"","content":"I always though that advancements were inventions that were not only of a much higher quality that their mundane equivalents, but also were decades ahead of what was possible with the level of technological and scientific development of the era. All this while still been rooted in what regular science and technology considers possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T18:05:13-07:00","id":157151,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a reasonable description of them, yes \u2014 with the caveat that they often go beyond the bounds of what regular science and technology considers possible, by being <i>too good</i> at what they do. The Rocketeer\u2019s jet-pack doesn\u2019t use Unobtainium Rocket Fuel, just a special blend of regular rocket fuel; but it manages to keep the Rocketeer aloft for impossibly long periods of time: realistically, a rocket pack using anything resembling normal rocket fuel would have exhausted its fuel tank before it could be used to do anything interesting. James Bond\u2019s spy-tech is another example of too-good-to-be-true technology: again, no exotic principles are invoked; but the gadgets that Q supplies him with are smaller and more effective than is realistically possible. <br /> <br /> <i>That\u2019s</i> what Talented Super-Science should focus on, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T07:16:22-07:00","id":157802,"title":"","content":"One of the things that rubs me the wrong way is how in a world were this kind of wonders are possible super scientists and their inventions don't have any kind of serious impact in society at large (I'm looking at you marvel and dc, Mister fantastic your genius only compares to your uselessness). Not the case with aberrant which I liked precisely because super geniuses used common sense, they became rich spreading their creations and using their intellect for practical problems instead of building lasers to destroy the moon and rule the world. However I found with adventure that the fact that the governments didn't use inspired and their super science, especially in the 2 world war, too forced to be true. The same goes for genius inspired who didn't use their abilities for profit or betterment of the world in a practical and realistic way. In the pulp era with all their wacky adventures I can suspend my disbelief and just enjoy the adventure since the ideals were different but in the second world war? with all the horror, the high stakes and the necessity? Inspired just disappeared and everybody ignored them?. However that is just my opinion but I would love to see a world in which the inspired truly made an impact and changed the landscape with their creations, what do you think?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T08:44:50-07:00","id":157875,"title":"","content":"Except, the DID try to use them in the Adventure! age. No one was interested. Ever heard of Harry Grindell Matthews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:59:37-07:00","id":158092,"title":"","content":"Oh, they were interested, alright. Understandably skeptical, but interested. It's just that whenever they asked Matthews to, ya' know, actually PROVE that his &quot;death ray&quot; did what he said it did under conditions the government would be satisfied with (as in beyond some dodgy &quot;demonstrations&quot; he set up that could have easily been staged), he kept refusing and running away. And claiming that people were bidding for his invention when they actually weren't.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, he was probably quite brilliant. He invented a selenium remote control device, and from what I can gather it could be interpreted that he didn't want any experts examining his inventions and stealing his designs. But he did act very suspiciously, and if it did work, he didn't seem particularly concerned with getting it out there unless he got his share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 06-03-2014, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:21:53-07:00","id":158102,"title":"","content":"In the real world, yeah, he might not have been the most reliable inventor. However, the stories we hear today about these things could prove useful when coming up with reasons for why these things never played out in the game history. Maybe he had built an Inspired device that really could do these things, but it was so advanced and unreliable that he had trouble getting it to work outside of laboratory conditions? Though I didn't have a chance to type up much with my last post, the point I had meant to make was that there is precedence for brilliant Inspired scientists to have their work potentially discredited or ignored by some people in the world. In the Aeonverse, most people who looked back at historical accounts of events and inventions from the Adventure! age believed them to simply be sensationalistic journalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:59:25-07:00","id":158258,"title":"","content":"I agree with you in that there are many ways in which you could justify it. People not taking them seriously, wary businessmen putting them down to avoid competition, too overly complicated inventions...etc. It's not an argument, it's more a personal taste, is just that as I grow older I become more inflexible with things I perceive as incoherent or that don't make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-03-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:05:55-07:00","id":158264,"title":"","content":"Any setting where drama trumps realism will look incoherent if you look at it too closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:29:49-07:00","id":158291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=158258#post158258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...wary businessmen putting them down to avoid competition...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's called &quot;Thomas Edison&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yeah, that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T16:55:10-07:00","id":158412,"title":"","content":"Yes I agree with you Data, after all this is a game, with too much realism and without any drama it would be boring as hell and look stupid. However you can be realistic without loosing drama. One example of this and an excellent super-heroic setting is <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godlike_(role-playing_game\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godlike_(role-playing_game</a>) and this <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Talents_(role-playing_game\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Ta...e-playing_game</a>). They have, at least in my opinion, one of the best super-powered backgrounds I have ever read. The reason is because they describe a world in which the existence of super-people and the consequences of their actions have a huge impact in society in a very realistic and coherent way without losing any epicness . I highly recommend it if you haven't read them before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-03-2014, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:24:30-07:00","id":159222,"title":"","content":"I never got a chance to run the Adeventure! era, but in my Aberrant games, Utopia's Tech Regulation department was a frequent antagonist. They were dedicated to keeping advancements &quot;the world was not ready for&quot; out of the hands of the general public and to keep the technological advancement curve to something approaching manageable.<br /> <br /> They were a fun complication because often times my players agreed with them. Not every brilliant innovation, even ones that were seemingly benign, would have a positive impact on a society already reeling under the strain of rapid, radical change.<br /> <br /> No reason to see why the Adventure! era wouldn't have a organization with a similar philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:33:31-07:00","id":159225,"title":"","content":"It actually did, in a much-less regulated sense. Typing on my phone so I can't get much out, but the party (almost always part of the Aeon Society) might occasionally run into the Rational Experimentation Group (I might have gotten the name wrong, any fact checkers?). Essentially, the REG was a &quot;Scientific progress, morals be damned&quot; group. They frequentlyexperimented on orphans, etc. Sold dangerous tech to the highest bidder. The Aeon Society sometimes tried to stop them from using science to hurt people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T06:31:58-07:00","id":159956,"title":"","content":"The REG as far as I have read in the book, are much like you described them Lustral. They represent the danger of super-science without any concern for the consequences. An organization that prevents new technologies from being implemented into the world because of greed, fear or genuine concern for the damage they could make makes a lot of sense. In fact it's ,at least for me, the main reason why super-technology wouldn't run rampant in the world. It's what the adventure! game lacks, a group that represents this ideal and directly opposes REG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T07:51:52-07:00","id":159983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=158258#post158258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wary businessmen putting them down to avoid competition</div> </div> </div> </div>This happens sometimes in the real world, so it isn't far-fetched at all. If a powerful industry is threatened by a new invention, they'll pull out the stops to prevent &quot;unfair&quot; competition from challenging their business model, no matter how beneficial it could have been for society. Electric cars, file sharing models for movies, and renewable energy have all been delayed compared to their potential, possibly in some cases by decades, because powerful industries try to stop them, often via their large political influence.<br /> <br /> Other inventions could have awful side effects (especially if folks like the REG developed them) that nobody really wants to put up with. Even one accident with a prototype could be enough to turn people off if it's a big, dangerous disaster that destroys a lot of property or kills a bunch of people. Imagine if the very first nuclear power plant had melted down and exploded in its first year of operation. Early setbacks and deaths have slowed down research in gene therapy, for example. Even fake awful side effects (such as the equivalent of the &quot;vaccines cause autism&quot; fraud) could have a similar effect if they get early and widespread publicity, regardless of what motivated the fraud itself.<br /> <br /> A third option is that the infrastructure overhaul necessary for widespread use is more expensive or difficult to set up than anyone wants, or requires a large supply of some limited or dangerous resource.<br /> <br /> Lastly, don't discount the possibility of religious or cultural movements in large enough numbers that simply resist or oppose new inventions for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, none of the examples I can think of have been scuttled, only delayed. But on the third appendage, I'm not likely to be aware of technologies that were never adopted at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-05-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T13:13:34-07:00","id":235701,"title":"","content":"The life and works of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla\" target=\"_blank\">Nikola Tesla</a> also might make some pretty good referential example of a super-genius meeting some pretty big hurdles in getting his wonders in the hands of the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:04:10-07:00","id":235746,"title":"","content":"I had Tesla in my Adventure! game. Many of my players would ask, &quot;Is he a Stalwart? A Mesmerist? A Daredevil? Is he a Nova? A Psiad? A PARAMORPH?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tesla,&quot; I would tell them, &quot;is Tesla.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:19:11-07:00","id":235754,"title":"","content":"Tesla actually appears in Adventure!, in one of the letters from Sarah Gettel. He has successfully opened a portal to another dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:19:42-07:00","id":235755,"title":"","content":"My games use the following from this site: <a href=\"http://swiki.fancruft.com/index.php?title=Aberrant_2.0_Mental_Systems\" target=\"_blank\">http://swiki.fancruft.com/index.php?...Mental_Systems</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">&quot;To fully clarify, there are three &quot;types&quot; of technical advancement in <i>Aberrant</i>. Conventional science, super-science, and Devices.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b>Conventional</b> science is stuff that fully meshes with the laws of physics and requires no exotic ingredients, nor does it play with the nigh-magical forces that the Inspired possess. Conventional science creates things like suborbitals, advanced body armor, railguns, powersuits, the occasional robot, fusion reactors, pollution-eating microbes, genetic enhancements, the list goes on and on. Anyone, baseline or Inspired, can advance conventional science.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b>Super-science</b> isn't the same thing as cutting edge science. It's research and development which requires exotic, Nova-created ingredients or perhaps uses Noetic or Quantum forces (as opposed to small-q quantum). Super-science can be duplicated by baselines with the right materials, but cannot be advanced by baselines. Super-science developments include FTL drives, Soma, Eufiber based infrastructure, hypercore rounds, and several varieties of free-floating active nanotech.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b>Devices</b> are handcrafted systems which are unique to the creator and their harnessing of Quantum or Noetic forces. Devices can be created by the Inspired but cannot be duplicated (although there are Devices that are similar enough to have identical game effects) because they are personal expressions of power, rather than technical advancements <i>per se</i>. In fact, some Devices may not even pretend to be scientific systems, rather being invested in power via pseudo-mystical New Age methods. The Haitian school of the Aesculpians is somewhat fond of using strange herbal concoctions as Vitakinetic devices, although how much of that is belief and how much of that is purposeful provocation of Montressor is unknown, and in the Nova Age there are many Novas who build fantastical magical wands and &quot;enchanted swords&quot; for interested parties with the money.&quot;</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:32:14-07:00","id":235763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=235754#post235754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tesla actually appears in Adventure!, in one of the letters from Sarah Gettel. He has successfully opened a portal to another dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did! I still recall the accompanying artwork of a creature staring through (I believe that was where the art appeared). He also refused to describe who was funding his portal tech. That machine appeared in one of my games -- led to a crossover story with a Technocracy game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:58:00-07:00","id":238193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=235763#post235763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He did! I still recall the accompanying artwork of a creature staring through (I believe that was where the art appeared). He also refused to describe who was funding his portal tech. That machine appeared in one of my games -- led to a crossover story with a Technocracy game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That must have been curious as Tesla was about as Son of Ether as one can get, afaik. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:02:07-07:00","id":238349,"title":"","content":"Ive been enjoying implementing Adventure!'s super science rules over Trinity's tech. My players love the idea of having their chief engineer locked away in his machine shop for a little while, only to come out with a new set of blaster pistols better than anything, or plans to increase their ships speed by 250%...making it the fastest in the galaxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:02:06-07:00","id":238644,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I'm not fond of the notion that super-science has no place in the Aeon Trinity era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:28:35-07:00","id":238662,"title":"","content":"Basically what we're saying is we need to surrender to our glorious Pulp Science Hero/Villain overlords here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:53:36-07:00","id":238677,"title":"","content":"Or &quot;space opera heroes and villains&quot;, in the case of Aeon Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:42:30-07:00","id":239100,"title":"","content":"Pfft, that's the same thing IN SPACE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:59:59-07:00","id":239129,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Adventure: Pulp Heroes</li> <li>Aberrant: Super-Heroes (i.e., Pulp Heroes WITH POWER!)</li> <li>Aeon: Space Opera Heroes (i.e., Pulp Heroes IN SPACE!)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-24-2014, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:03:44-07:00","id":240868,"title":"","content":"I never saw Aberrant and Aeon as pulpy at all, to be honest.<br /> <br /> In fact, Aberrant stems from superhero comics that are very much <i>not</i> pulpy.<br /> <br /> You don't fight jetpack apes, you fight global warming/capitalism/etc, taking part in global idealogical conflicts. Aeon is like that but in the future, more of a serious business sci-fi setting than a pulpy planetary romance setting.<br /> <br /> That Aberrant is not pulpy is one of the things I love about it most, actually, as most superhero RPGs are very pulpy indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T17:32:57-07:00","id":240912,"title":"","content":"I guess my view of Aberrant is skewed, because the only game of it I've played has equal doses pulp and 'serious business' swirled together. And my only experience with Aeon (Trinity, then) was cannibalizing pieces of it for Aberrant and Adventure!, since I wasn't very fond of it on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T00:43:47-07:00","id":243722,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m expecting the Trinity Continuum to focus more on being larger-than-life than most of Trinity Universe did. For instance: if TC still has Dramatic Editing rules at all, I expect that they\u2019ll be available in <i>all eras</i>, not just <b>Adventure!</b>. I expect that <b>Abberant</b> will be a mixture of \u201cpulp\u201d and \u201cserious business\u201d, as Aiden put it, rather than being a purely Watchmen-like deconstruction of superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:51:02-07:00","id":243928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=243722#post243722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m expecting the Trinity Continuum to focus more on being larger-than-life than most of Trinity Universe did. For instance: if TC still has Dramatic Editing rules at all, I expect that they\u2019ll be available in <i>all eras</i>, not just <b>Adventure!</b>. I expect that <b>Abberant</b> will be a mixture of \u201cpulp\u201d and \u201cserious business\u201d, as Aiden put it, rather than being a purely Watchmen-like deconstruction of superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's probably time to move past the deconstructionism, because the deconstructions of the deconstructions have now been deconstructed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:00:25-07:00","id":244106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=243928#post243928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the deconstructions of the deconstructions have now been deconstructed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To understand recursion, one must first understand recursion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:48:19-07:00","id":244177,"title":"","content":"According to the Gencon panel, they're looking to expand the genres Aberrant and Adventure! cover, so Aberrant covers more superhero territory and Adventure! more pulp territory (they're fine with the breadth of stuff Aeon/Trinity covers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:03:59-07:00","id":244187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=244106#post244106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To understand recursion, one must first understand recursion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the dictionary under &quot;redundant&quot; it says &quot;see redundant&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:13:21-07:00","id":244314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=244177#post244177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Gencon panel, they're looking to expand the genres Aberrant and Adventure! cover, so Aberrant covers more superhero territory and Adventure! more pulp territory (they're fine with the breadth of stuff Aeon/Trinity covers).</div> </div> </div> </div>They may be fine with the breadth of \u00c6on/Trinity; but I wish it was broader, with more protagonist options than just \u201cpsions\u201d and more support for Planetary Romance and/or Space Opera chronicles (the former being supported by playing up such things as Martian and Lunar culture, the latter being supported by providing support for the likes of Dramatic Editing and Super-Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:51:02-07:00","id":244333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=244314#post244314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They may be fine with the breadth of \u00c6on/Trinity; but I wish it was broader, with more protagonist options than just \u201cpsions\u201d and more support for Planetary Romance and/or Space Opera chronicles (the former being supported by playing up such things as Martian and Lunar culture, the latter being supported by providing support for the likes of Dramatic Editing and Super-Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what we're saying is we want our Barsoom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:24:58-07:00","id":244370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=244333#post244333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically what we're saying is we want our Barsoom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn straight!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:04:06-07:00","id":244666,"title":"","content":"For me, going space opera/planetary romance would be a better fit for Adventure! and/or for a time period after Aeon, rather than Aeon itself. (Which is not to argue against having genre-appropriate dramatic editing and super-science in Aeon; I've got no problem with that.)<br /> <br /> Basically, Aeon has a particular Earth-centred focus, and the sci-fi subgenres it draws on are generally those that can be applied to an Earth-centred setting - cyberpunk, post-apocalypse, military sci-fi, first contact, first colonies, etc. Space opera and planetary romance are generally _not_ Earth-centric in focus - they're more about exciting adventure in outer space or on other worlds, so they'd be a better match for Adventure!, which is all about the exciting adventure, or somewhere further forwards in time, when Earth's concerns aren't the focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:23:38-07:00","id":245556,"title":"","content":"Ive been running an Adventure! game set in the year 2550, using trinity tech including the &quot;top secret&quot; and prototype stuff as the norm for technology. Space travel is handled by having each alien species having an FTL capability (hyper drive, gravity well manipulation, etc) except for humanity who has become relient on &quot;jump gates&quot;, giant rings that respond to human dna and allow for near Instant travel up to 17 A.U. placed all over space by aberrants before the great war of 2070. By using all this tech but with adventures rules, the pc's really feel like they get into and out of situations that would work as video game cutscenes or movies. They laugh and talk about things like they just saw it in the last nolan flick...which makes me happy, but lets me know that rhey are in a sometimes serious, sometimes silly but always action packed space epic ala 5th element or serenity meets mass effect or star wars. Also-give a dynamic a vibro sword, and silk steel, a heroic a high threat combat rifle, and a mesmerist access to bio computers...its good fun all around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:25:48-07:00","id":245558,"title":"","content":"Ahh, and to update the tech by near 500 years, adjust the speed of VS 5 in the old books to the new VS 1 and make olaminium still expensive, but readily available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T10:25:45-08:00","id":333199,"title":"","content":"Super science has a role to play in all of the games - although i dare say the order i prefer is counter-intuitive with Adventure! seeing a relaxed approach to hard science (in my mind because of the Hammersmith effect's temporal proximity), in the Nova age mega-Intelligence bends the rules again, but we see some Novas being attuned to certain forces capable of inventions another Nova of similar intelligence and power but a different anima (suite of powers) couldn't attain and vice versa. Then in the future where things should be more advanced, you have Black-Technologies innovated by Novas being supressed and more hard science as befits a science-fiction setting.<br /> I would actually like to see more theoretical science described in the Aeon/Trinity end of the arc; Nanotech, AI, Time-Tubes and even a few uplifted species or transhuman recipes/rigs/emulators/implants might have been innovated by Novas and suffer heavy research restrictions. But the information while tightly regulated should be available through the Trinity gate-keepers in the interest of advancing stable science - some places like the Colony haunted asteroid belt may still be developing these technologies in frightfully isolated and under-patrolled bernal spheres where technology laws matter little.<br /> I certainly feel the future end of the aeonverse has room for more transhumanism as a kind of variant to Psion characters or baselines. I'm not sugesting you openly rip off Transhuman Space, but i would like to see the scope widened for that possibility. After all Whitley Styles is still around in 2121 or 2122 - so the Trinity are aware if not particularly generous with the technology for enhancing human capacities. The only detailed cyberware was found in Asia Ascendant - which was never published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T15:22:03-08:00","id":333483,"title":"","content":"To be fair, we don\u2019t know that Whitley Styles is still around in the \u00c6on era of the Trinity <i>Continuum</i> (as opposed to the Trinity <i>Universe</i> \u2014 that is, the new game as opposed to the old ones). Likewise, science fiction can range from hard science to space opera; and in general, the presence of psionic powers tends to align more with the space opera end rather than the hard science end. Heck, given what has been leaked about the nature of Talents, my suspicion is that the TC as a whole is going to lean more toward the space opera side: that is, the relaxed approach to science is going to be more or less omnipresent. Remember, the default setting in the TC core book is going to feature modern-day Talents; so the loosened strictures of Adventure aren\u2019t <i>unique</i> to the Adventure era. <br /> <br /> All that said: I agree about wanting the \u00c6on era to have a more developed scientific baseline than the Aberrant era (with new technologies that do <i>not</i> depend on Noetic or \u201cQuantum\u201d principles to operate), just as the Aberrant era has a more advanced baseline than the Adventure era. And to the extent that Talents have access to superscience, it should take the form of being able to play fast and loose with the precise limitations of any given era\u2019s scientific baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T19:53:19-08:00","id":333688,"title":"","content":"Okay, first point is valid, but really what we do know is contained on a short point by point document. I thought perhaps using the original setting might have made for a useful guideline - that's what brought me here after all.<br /> I'm aware of the genres of Sci-Fi and while hard science is my preference (and not necessarily exclusive of space opera), the boat sailed on that a long time ago for the Aeonverse - but i've always preferred the technology to be at least theoretically possible if humanity is going to get a hold on it - or at least well described, like the noetic principles we were given in various old supplements. Even then, the old Nova-tech and older inspired devices <i>are</i> indivisible from the greater setting - Trinity era games have artificially hardened science - which is about all i can hope for given the &quot;What we Know&quot; document (which finally loaded for me after all my posts last night).<br /> Talents? This is a new term for daredevils/paramorphs, i take it? I am still missing some of the information taken for granted here i suspect. Further investigation will be embarked upon.<br /> It's not a question of mechanics as much as one of genre and style differences between the eras - i have no problem with inventions modifying numbers or effects to some extent that seems fair and fun, but i don't think Jekyll/Hyde potions, frankenstein monsters, pedal powered flying machines, energy shields or any other unforeseen advances in science should be bandied about too liberally in the sci-fi end of the story. That said, process 418, by my understanding of how this stuff works, is going to change all that anyway. But i still would argue that this is a matter of genre and not a flat out limitation on the mechanics.<br /> E.G. Light-speed comes up regularly in Sci-Fi, sometimes in Superhero stories and rarely if ever in Pulp - the three genres demand different approaches to science. Sometimes pulp-/super-heroes even veer into mysticism too, although i doubt it would fit in the ultra-slick Aberrant setting as written.<br /> The Aeonverse is so versatile in it's genre that these things can cross over to contrast with common contraptions of the age - but it should be done sparingly and with reason - if only to preserve mood and intent of the setting material. If the players prefer a looser, pulpy approach to their space-faring - then the GM/ST/whatever this system calls it should see the desire and shift the genre accordingly. Same when they prefer a more codified framework of possibilities. I would urge a baseline equipment list steeped in hard science as often as practical, so that <i>players</i> can be the ones to innovate the FTL drive, energy shield or pseudo gravity generator. Thereby letting the hard science fans such as myself to run the setting without pruning out parts of hard-wired rules and assumptions. At least that's what i personally hope for concerning super-science.<br /> The lapses in hard science within the 2120's are mostly well reasoned out anyway; with Psionics being an alien gift, along with the chambers, noetic biotech and jump-drive technology with other culprits such as Nova tech (being encased in quantum taint away from the noetic universe) and earlier relics (created in a period of altered physical reality).<br /> I understand that we are branching into more eras now, but that simply means i can't guess at what the breadth of inspired innovation for those eras might be and this becomes Schrodinger's point, hidden beyond the terminator. So forgive me for clinging to what i know for now.<br /> Outside of these special circumstances the technology attributed to pure human development has followed a fairly realistic model - with attention paid to orbital mechanics, reaction fuel and bandwidth - elements that rarely trouble full-flight space opera, which operates more like pulp in space <i>at times</i>. It would be a shame to loose that aspect of the setting because a biokinetic psion can turn his head into a fern or a Talent/Paramorph can return from certain death.<br /> <br /> I do hope i'm making sense in between all this ranting. Let me summarize:<br /> The boat sailed long ago for pure science - but there is no need to throw the baby out with the bathwater. Especially when the genre is Bab-Fi.<br /> Or something along those lines.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> I better go and find the part where daredevils became Talents now, thanks for the response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T08:59:01-08:00","id":347466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=157802#post157802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that rubs me the wrong way is how in a world were this kind of wonders are possible super scientists and their inventions don't have any kind of serious impact in society at large (I'm looking at you marvel and dc, Mister fantastic your genius only compares to your uselessness). Not the case with aberrant which I liked precisely because super geniuses used common sense, they became rich spreading their creations and using their intellect for practical problems instead of building lasers to destroy the moon and rule the world. However I found with adventure that the fact that the governments didn't use inspired and their super science, especially in the 2 world war, too forced to be true. The same goes for genius inspired who didn't use their abilities for profit or betterment of the world in a practical and realistic way. In the pulp era with all their wacky adventures I can suspend my disbelief and just enjoy the adventure since the ideals were different but in the second world war? with all the horror, the high stakes and the necessity? Inspired just disappeared and everybody ignored them?. However that is just my opinion but I would love to see a world in which the inspired truly made an impact and changed the landscape with their creations, what do you think?.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Mr. Fantastic's defense most of the stuff he's good at involves dimensional/temporal anomalies, rifts and stuff that, without an exploration team composed overpowered explorers like the FF, would probably result in the shattering of the planet or its devastation/takeover by who knows how many varieties of aliens or near-lovecraftian cosmic horrors. That and trying to deal with weird colaterals of cosmic radiation in his team seem to be his strong suits (and should be said, he has admited more than once that Banner and Octavius are better than him at it).<br /> <br /> Unstable molecules uniforms, maybe Herbie, might be the only <b>pratical</b> invention he ever did.<br /> <br /> If you can, try sometime to check the &quot;Reed Richards Guide to Everything&quot;, for Marvel Super Heroes: Saga Edition (late 90s) for a very entertaining work and read on a super-scientist's interactions with the world and other stuff.<br /> <br /> Tony Stark &amp; Lex Luthor are the geniuses that might be said to be &quot;more down to earth&quot; in their specialties areas and inventions - for all the good it does (not do) to the world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-29-2014, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T06:38:08-08:00","id":355706,"title":"","content":"Far and away, the best RPG book for superhumans tranforming the setting is Progenitor. The best comics are newuniversal (for the early days) and Supergod (for the latter days).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 12-31-2014, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T07:11:35-08:00","id":355734,"title":"","content":"I am beyond excited about everything you just said Neall. Progenitor is THE game for the effects of superhuman abilities in a real world setting, especially the use of Mega Attributes. I especially like the &quot;automatic abilities&quot; that come with high levels of intellect and the use of syntergenic engineering. NewUniversal is perfect for the introduction of high powered supers and SuperGod shows what multiple high level Novas such as Mal can do to a setting. My incredibly high expectations just jumped a little higher. No pressure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:25:52-08:00","id":355890,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamRice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/157105-super-science-in-trinity-continuum?p=355734#post355734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am beyond excited about everything you just said Neall. Progenitor is THE game for the effects of superhuman abilities in a real world setting, especially the use of Mega Attributes. I especially like the &quot;automatic abilities&quot; that come with high levels of intellect and the use of syntergenic engineering. NewUniversal is perfect for the introduction of high powered supers and SuperGod shows what multiple high level Novas such as Mal can do to a setting. My incredibly high expectations just jumped a little higher. No pressure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Progenitor? sorry but I don't think so, It is a great setting but for me the one and only &quot;realistic&quot; superpowered setting is wild talents. No other game describes the impact of superpowers and comic book characters in real life so well and with such an amazing story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T13:52:32-08:00","id":356015,"title":"","content":"The &quot;World Gone Mad&quot; setting (the Wild Talents core) is another favorite of mine, so I certainly won't argue that it isn't great. For me though, Progenitor captured the social and technological ramifications in a more realistic manner considering the high powered supers involved (which is my favorite part of any superhuman setting). But you really can't go wrong with an Arc Dream setting, Grim War and Kerberos Club are other great examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}